      "intent": {"task": "Enumerate both real solutions of the symmetric triple/product system.", "source_solution": "a_3=1 from the sum. (1-d)(1+d)=-8 gives d^2=9, so d=3 or -3. a_1=1-2d yields (-5,3) and (7,-3).", "unit_reason": "Both branches solve one nonlinear system; native multiple selection preserves the complete solution set without a combination code.", "concept_blocks": [5], "limitations": ["Selection cannot establish independently deriving the quadratic relation and enumerating its roots."], "figure_observations": []},
      "key": {"correct": ["A", "D"], "rationales": [
        {"option_id": "A", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "a_2=-2,a_3=1,a_4=4 give sum 3 and product -8.", "misconception": null},
        {"option_id": "B", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "With a_1=1,d=3, the triple is 4,7,10, sum 21 and product 40.", "misconception": "Report the fixed middle term a_3=1 as the first term after finding d=3."},
        {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Use d=9 from d^2=9, then a_1=1-2(9)=-17. The triple -8,1,10 has outside product -80.", "misconception": "Remove the square without taking a square root."},
        {"option_id": "D", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "a_2=4,a_3=1,a_4=-2 give sum 3 and product -8, realizing d=-3.", "misconception": null}
      ]}
    },
    {
      "id": "q243-formula-membership", "source_numbers": ["243"],
      "view": {"mode": "single", "stem": "等差数列 $(x_n)$ 的首项为 $1.7$，公差为 $0.3$。哪一组正确给出通项、值 $32$ 与 $46.7$ 对应的序号，以及值 $62.7$ 是否为数列项的判断？", "figure_ids": [], "options": [
        {"id": "A", "text": "$x_n=0.3n+1.7$；序号分别为 $101,150$；$62.7$ 对应 $n=\\frac{610}{3}$，不是数列的项。", "figure_ids": []},
        {"id": "B", "text": "$x_n=0.3n+1.4$；序号分别为 $102,151$；$62.7$ 对应 $n=\\frac{613}{3}$，不是数列的项。", "figure_ids": []},
        {"id": "C", "text": "$x_n=0.3n+1.4$；序号分别为 $102,151$；$62.7$ 对应 $n=204$，是数列的项。", "figure_ids": []},
        {"id": "D", "text": "$x_n=0.3n+1.4$；序号分别为 $102,151$；$62.7$ 对应 $n=\\frac{613}{3}$，是数列的项。", "figure_ids": []}
      ]},
      "intent": {"task": "Retain the formula, both exact positions and the nonmembership proof criterion as one complete result.", "source_solution": "x_n=0.3n+1.4. Solving for n gives 102,151,613/3 respectively. The last is not an integer; x_204=62.6 and x_205=62.9.", "unit_reason": "All membership decisions depend on the same derived formula and integer-index condition; separating them would sever their common reasoning.", "concept_blocks": [5], "limitations": ["Recognition of a noninteger index argument cannot establish independently writing the required proof or formula."], "figure_observations": []},
      "key": {"correct": ["B"], "rationales": [
        {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "With mistaken x_n=1.7+0.3n, solving gives (32-1.7)/0.3=101, (46.7-1.7)/0.3=150 and (62.7-1.7)/0.3=610/3.", "misconception": "Use n increments from the first term; all subsequent positions inherit the shifted formula."},
        {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Expand 1.7+0.3(n-1); solve the three equations exactly; only 613/3 fails positive integrality.", "misconception": null},
        {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Truncate 613/3 to 204, although substituting gives x_204=62.6, not 62.7.", "misconception": "Round a real equation solution to an integer and assert exact membership."},
        {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The fractional root 613/3 solves the real equation but is not an admissible term index.", "misconception": "Accept every positive real root as a sequence index."}
      ]}
    },
    {
