    {
      "id": "q248-mixed-difference", "source_numbers": ["248"],
      "view": {"mode": "single", "stem": "数列由 $b_n=2n+3$ 给出，$k,n$ 为独立的正整数。哪一项正确给出 $b_2-b_1$、$b_{10}-b_9$、$b_{k+1}-b_n$，以及是否为等差数列的判断？", "figure_ids": [], "options": [
        {"id": "A", "text": "三个差依次为 $2,2,2$；任意 $n$ 有 $b_{n+1}-b_n=2$，是等差数列。", "figure_ids": []},
        {"id": "B", "text": "三个差依次为 $2,2,2(k+1-n)$；任意 $n$ 有 $b_{n+1}-b_n=2$，是等差数列。", "figure_ids": []},
        {"id": "C", "text": "三个差依次为 $2,2,2(n-k-1)$；任意 $n$ 有 $b_{n+1}-b_n=2$，是等差数列。", "figure_ids": []},
        {"id": "D", "text": "三个差依次为 $2,2,2(k-n)$；任意 $n$ 有 $b_{n+1}-b_n=2$，是等差数列。", "figure_ids": []}
      ]},
      "intent": {"task": "Retain the printed mixed-index difference, both numerical differences and the universal adjacent-difference criterion.", "source_solution": "The first two differences are 2. The mixed difference is [2(k+1)+3]-(2n+3)=2(k+1-n). Only after separately setting k=n does it become the adjacent difference 2, proving arithmeticity.", "unit_reason": "The general difference and adjacent specialization must be judged together to prevent conflating independent and equal indices.", "concept_blocks": [5], "limitations": ["Selecting a universal adjacent-difference argument does not establish independently producing the proof."], "figure_observations": []},
      "key": {"correct": ["B"], "rationales": [
        {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Substitute k=n prematurely and simplify 2(k+1-n) to 2. For k=2,n=1 the actual mixed difference is b_3-b_1=9-5=4.", "misconception": "Silently replace the independent k by n before evaluating the printed expression."},
        {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "7-5=2,23-21=2; subtract the general formulas to obtain 2(k+1-n), whose k=n specialization is always 2.", "misconception": null},
        {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "For the mixed expression subtract b_(k+1) from b_n instead: (2n+3)-[2(k+1)+3]=2(n-k-1).", "misconception": "Reverse the order only in the symbolic subtraction."},
        {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Replace b_(k+1) by 2k+3, then subtract 2n+3 to get 2(k-n).", "misconception": "Ignore the +1 inside the first term's index."}
      ]}
    }
    ,
    {
      "id": "q249-affine-proofs", "source_numbers": ["249"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "multiple",
        "stem": "分别考虑通项为 $y_n=2n-5$、$y_n=-3n+2$、$y_n=5n+1$、$y_n=10-7n$ 的四个数列，$n$ 为正整数。选出同时正确给出首项、公差及任意相邻项差的陈述。",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "$y_n=2n-5$：$y_1=-3$，$d=2$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=2$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "$y_n=-3n+2$：$y_1=-1$，$d=3$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=3$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "$y_n=5n+1$：$y_1=1$，$d=5$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=5$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "D", "text": "$y_n=10-7n$：$y_1=3$，$d=-7$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=-7$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "E", "text": "$y_n=2n-5$：$y_1=-5$，$d=2$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=2$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "F", "text": "$y_n=-3n+2$：$y_1=-1$，$d=-3$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=-3$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "G", "text": "$y_n=5n+1$：$y_1=6$，$d=5$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=5$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "H", "text": "$y_n=10-7n$：$y_1=3$，$d=7$，任意 $n$ 有 $y_{n+1}-y_n=7$。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Judge the first term and signed universal adjacent difference for all four affine formulas, thereby retaining the arithmeticity argument.",
        "source_solution": "For y_n=pn+q, y_1=p+q and y_(n+1)-y_n=p. The four parameter pairs are (-3,2),(-1,-3),(6,5),(3,-7), and each difference is independent of n.",
        "unit_reason": "The four formulas instantiate the same affine-to-progression characterization. One set of complete claims preserves every formula and its proof criterion, not separate clicks for each parameter.",
        "concept_blocks": [5],
        "limitations": ["Selecting universal difference claims does not demonstrate independently composing the requested four proofs."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {"correct": ["A", "D", "F", "G"], "rationales": [
        {"option_id": "A", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "y_1=2-5=-3 and [2(n+1)-5]-(2n-5)=2.", "misconception": null},
        {"option_id": "B", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The actual difference is -3. Expanding -3(n+1) incorrectly as -3n+3 produces the asserted +3 while the first term remains -1.", "misconception": "Lose the minus sign on the added constant when distributing -3 over n+1."},
        {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "y_1=5(1)+1=6, not 1; the adjacent difference 5 is otherwise correct.", "misconception": "Use the affine intercept y_0=1 as the first term."},
        {"option_id": "D", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "y_1=10-7=3 and [10-7(n+1)]-(10-7n)=-7.", "misconception": null},
        {"option_id": "E", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "y_1=2-5=-3, not -5; the proposed -5 is the value at n=0.", "misconception": "Identify the intercept with the first term."},
        {"option_id": "F", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "y_1=-3+2=-1 and [-3(n+1)+2]-(-3n+2)=-3.", "misconception": null},
        {"option_id": "G", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "y_1=5+1=6 and [5(n+1)+1]-(5n+1)=5.", "misconception": null},
        {"option_id": "H", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The actual adjacent difference is -7. Mistakenly expand -7(n+1) as -7n+7 to obtain +7.", "misconception": "Distribute the negative coefficient with the wrong sign on the constant increment."}
      ]}
